CORE
unknown.c
--stop-on-fail --sarif-result -
activate-multi-line-match
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
"kind": "open"
"text": "undecided under stop-on-fail \(UNKNOWN\)"
"propertyId": "main\.assertion\.1"
"kind": "fail"
"level": "error"
"propertyId": "main\.assertion\.2"
--
"level": "(note|none|warning)"
--
Checks the UNKNOWN -> open SARIF mapping: under --stop-on-fail an undecided
property is reported with kind "open" and no level (SARIF 2.1.0 3.27.10 only
permits level "none" for kinds other than "fail"), while the failing property
is reported with kind "fail" and level "error".
